---
source: crates/biome_yaml_analyze/tests/spec_tests.rs
expression: invalidAliases.yaml
---
# Input
```yaml
# should generate diagnostics
plain: &plain true
tagged: &tagged !!bool "true"
tagged_mapping: &mapping !!bool
  key: value
first_key:
  &first false: 1

? *plain
: 2
? *tagged
: 3
? *mapping
: 4
flow: { *plain : 5, *first : 6 }

# the alias refers to the closest anchor before it
again: &again text
other: &again True
? *again
: 7

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalidAliases.yaml:7:10 lint/nursery/noYamlBooleanKeys ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This key is a boolean, not text.
  
    5 │   key: value
    6 │ first_key:
  > 7 │   &first false: 1
      │          ^^^^^
    8 │ 
    9 │ ? *plain
  
  i YAML reads this unquoted word as a boolean value. Tools that read this file can reject boolean keys, or convert them to text that differs from what is written here.
  
  i Wrap the key in quotes to keep it as text.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

